    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\left( 10y^{6} \\right)^{5}$\n\nWrite $100000=10^5$ to find the outer index, then solve $5m=30$ for the inner index.",
      "worked": "$100000=10^5$, so the outside exponent is $5$. The inside exponent satisfies $5m=30$, so $m=6$. Thus $(10y^6)^5=100000y^{30}$.",
